          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Kolmogorov product
            is a way of forming infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicartesian+monoidal+category"} semicartesian monoidal category
            which is not necessarily
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            it coincides with the usual infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            (if it exists).
          %p
            If the category in question is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %span.newWikiWord
              finitary complete monoid
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/finitary+complete+monoid"} ?
            structure (up to reversing the arrows).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In what follows, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\otimes 1)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicartesian+monoidal+category"} semicartesian monoidal category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2
            be objects of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo !
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
